When an EXCEPT answer is about a different sense or a different kind of evidence than the paradox (hearing vs. seeing), it's usually the one that doesn't help.$pilot$), ($pilot$C$pilot$, $pilot$This answer says, "It's rarely seen because it sits frozen while the small birds dash around." Movement catches the eye. Still birds are much harder to spot.$pilot$), ($pilot$D$pilot$, $pilot$This answer says, "It's rarely seen because it's active at night, while bird-watchers are out during the day."$pilot$), ($pilot$E$pilot$, $pilot$This answer says, "It's rarely seen because it stays alone and only flies when it's in danger, while the small birds fly around in groups all day." Flocks in the air are easy to spot. A bird that stays hidden in the grass isn't.$pilot$)) v(letter,body) WHERE q.qid=$pilot$PT109-S3-Q3$pilot$ AND e.style='single' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM lr_explanation_choice_notes n WHERE n.explanation_id=e.id) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

